    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m somewhat puzzled by the following. Both Lavaan and Mplus converge, but I&#39;m puzzled that the LL is different and that the paramter estimates are so different. The example I show here is 300 observations, six variables and no missing data.<div>I&#39;ve attached the lavaan program (factormeanshift.R), the Mplus program (fmshift2.inp) and the data (sixtimegrowth.txt). Any ideas? thanks! Phil</div><div> <div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"238\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:178pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"103\" style=\"width:77pt\">\r\n <col width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">\r\n <col width=\"71\" style=\"width:53pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"103\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:77pt\">Estimates</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">Mplus</td>\r\n  <td width=\"71\" style=\"width:53pt\">Lavaan</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">ChiSquare</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1102.944</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\"><span style=\"text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap;border-spacing:0px\">1144.796</span></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">df</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">13</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">13</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">Factor Loadings</td>\r\n  <td></td>\r\n  <td></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">T0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0.865</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.068</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">T1</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0.86</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1.063</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0p